\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{One velocity at the present state}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The equations of \ref{fnip-0005} give
#{(\dot V,\dot n)} at the present pair #{(V,n)}. The curve in
\ref{fnip-0011} is one solution of those equations. A second solution
with the same value at time #{0} would be a second way for that pair
to move. The time along the drawn curve is a finite window, and the
question is how that window is chosen.}
